      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T18:30:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you elaborate the reasoning here for the scope change? I feel like having them separate is not a big issue and should still work fine, and actually can be better in some cases, like mapping from a set pointer to its info. The pool structure already has `allocedSetsToBoxed` to perform operations over the sets when needed and having 1-1 mapping between the vulkan handles to info structures just feels natural.",
      "revId": "f3d14c0a3412e1d4c8a6115c895fbf7c87328a4c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8043ec07_262d090a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1128973
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T18:44:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reasoning is all of these mappings have an incorrect assumption; that vulkan handles are globally unique. This is actually not a guarantee, as Bo and I have observed, and is also not clearly defined in the Vulkan spec. The only guarantee that we have is that VkInstances are unique as it is a per-application state object.\n\nFor example, we\u0027ve seen VkDevices handles with the exact same unboxed handles, but coming from different VkInstances. This problem is actually why we have vkDestroyFence crashes (VkDevice handle collisions).\n\nThe scoping refactor (this CL would be the first of many) will correctly put all of the objects in the proper hierarchy, so that unboxed Vulkan handles can co-exist without these collisions, and we can clean up correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "3f7f2c81_909e45b5",
      "revId": "f3d14c0a3412e1d4c8a6115c895fbf7c87328a4c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "51982ee7_42d5246a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561731
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T21:49:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this applies all handles, what do you think about keeping the `mDescriptorSetInfo` as is but then moving everything into per-instance/per-device structs?\n\n```\nstruct DeviceInfo {\n  std::mutex mMutex;\n  std::unordered_map\u003cVkBuffer, BufferInfo\u003e mBufferInfos GUARDED_BY(mMutex);\n  std::unordered_map\u003cVkImage, ImageInfo\u003e mImageInfos GUARDED_BY(mMutex);\n  ...\n  std::unordered_map\u003cVkDescriptorSet, DescriptorSetInfo\u003e mDescriptorSetInfos GUARDED_BY(mMutex);\n};\n\nstruct InstanceInfo {\n  std::mutex mMutex;  \n  std::unordered_map\u003cVkDevice, DeviceInfo\u003e mDeviceInfos GUARDED_BY(mMutex);\n};\n\nclass VkDecoderGlobalState::Impl {\n  private:\n    std::mutex mMutex;\n    std::unordered_map\u003cVkInstance, InstanceInfo\u003e mInstanceInfos GUARDED_BY(mMutex);\n}\n```\n\nI suppose this might also allow us to have finer grain locking -  instead of everything holding onto the global lock.",
      "parentUuid": "8043ec07_262d090a",
      "revId": "f3d14c0a3412e1d4c8a6115c895fbf7c87328a4c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
